course: dictionary
lesson: 14183
title: Mono: one, or short for something else
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word mono can mean different things, so check the clues in the sentence to see which one it means. At the start of a word, mono- means one or single: «The train ran on a monorail, with just one track.»
explain: «The old film was in mono, so all the sound came from one speaker.» Here mono is about sound: one channel, not left and right like stereo. «Ben had mono and stayed in bed for a week.» Here mono is short for an illness, so the words stayed in bed are the clue.
explain: Mono can also be short for monochrome, which means one colour, like black and white. When you meet mono, ask what the sentence is about: sound, health, or one thing? Then swap in your meaning and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Mono- at the start of a word means one or single.
fact: «Monorail» means a railway with one track; «monologue» means a speech by one person.
fact: In sound, «mono» means one channel, the opposite of stereo.
fact: In health, «mono» is short for mononucleosis, an illness that makes you very tired with a sore throat; in the UK it is called glandular fever.
fact: «Monochrome» means one colour, often black and white.
exercise: «The train ran along a monorail with only one track.» What does mono- mean in monorail? | *One or single | Very fast | Made of metal | Two
exercise: «The film was shown in mono, so every sound came from one speaker.» What does mono mean here? | An illness | A colour, like red | A type of train | *A single channel of sound, the opposite of stereo
exercise: «Her drawing was in monochrome, all black and white.» What does monochrome mean here? | *One colour, like black and white | Very colourful | Covered in paint | Very bright
test: «Ben had mono, so he was tired and had a sore throat for weeks.» What is mono short for here? | Monochrome | Monologue | Monorail | *Mononucleosis, an illness
test: In «monotone», what does mono- mean? | *One or single | Happy | Loud | Many
exam: Ayesha reads «a monologue by one actor» and says mono means two. What is the right meaning? | Mono means a sound from two speakers | *Mono- means one or single, so a monologue is one person speaking | Mono means many people talking | Ayesha is right, mono means two
